# --- secure-my-app's own state ---
# secure-my-app writes its whole audit into <project>/.secure-my-app/: the findings report, the request
# that proves each finding, the re-run log for every applied fix, and the raw responses it read
# to reach a verdict. Those files quote real hosts, real headers, real tokens and, when the
# finding IS a leaked credential, the credential itself. A findings report is also a map of
# what still works: committing one publishes the exploit before the fix lands. Never commit it,
# in this repo or in the project being audited; keep this repo generic.
.secure-my-app/
.goal/

# --- OS / editor noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
*.code-workspace

# --- Tooling ---
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.cache/
.omc/
.claude/

# build journal (local resumability only)
docs/audit/

